I replied to two issues and left the rest alone.

• #1120 (closed): Commit a4c72965 fixes it. When a DNS lookup fails for a reserved test name (.invalid, .test, .example, .localhost), yoyo now stops retrying. On the built binary, the repro from the issue went from 1m04s (six attempts) to 7.4s. Ordinary DNS failures still get the full retries, since a real resolver outage can recover. The ordinary-failure case is covered only by the table test; I didn't probe it live.
• #1100 (kept open): The yoagent upgrade (1b56d8cf) doesn't fix this. Its new group kill only fires while yoyo is alive to see the exit, and kill_group is still private. A fix still needs either a way upstream to get the server's process id, or yoyo saving that id when it connects.
